## 📈 Maverick Critical Analysis

| Platform | Primary Takeaway | Strategic Recommendation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **mRNA** | Highest neutralising antibody induction | Primary choice for boosters |
| **Adenoviral** | Slower logistics / Strong T-cell response | Heterologous mRNA boost recommended |
| **Protein** | Slower waning than viral vectors | Ideal for mRNA contraindications |
| **Inactivated** | High safety / Rapid effectiveness decay | Frequent boosting required |

---

## 💡 Strategic Synthesis

**Durability of Immunity**
Vaccine Effectiveness (VE) typically wanes by **6-8% per month** after month 3. The Maverick AI recommends a proactive booster schedule using heterologous platforms to maximize cross-neutralization of emerging variants.

> [!TIP]
> **Booster Strategy:** Heterologous boosting (e.g., J&J primary → Pfizer/Moderna boost) yields comparable or slightly higher neutralising titres than homologous schedules.

---

## 🛡️ Safety & Risk Profile

\boxed{The risk-benefit profile for all authorized vaccines remains strongly favorable, with severe adverse events (Myocarditis, TTS) occurring in fewer than 1 in 20,000 individuals, while protection against hospitalization exceeds 90% when boosted.}

